Many thanks to g2-kit-unofficial: https://github.com/Commute773/g2-kit-unofficial/
and others who contributed to documenting the G2's bluetooth protocol. It has enabled me
to keep my room clean, so to speak.

Voice wake-word detection uses sherpa-onnx: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/
and the sherpa-onnx KWS Zipformer GigaSpeech model published by the k2-fsa/sherpa
community.

G2 microphone LC3 decoding uses Google's liblc3: https://github.com/google/liblc3

The optional TerminusV proportional font is by ohnonot, derived from Dimitar
Zhekov's Terminus: https://framagit.org/ohnonot/terv-terc
It is distributed under the SIL Open Font License; see
app/fonts/terminusv/LICENSE.
